# Changelog

## libvt 0.1.x (Yet to be released)

<!-- KEEP THIS PLACEHOLDER - DO NOT REMOVE OR MODIFY THIS LINE -->
_Notes on the upcoming release will go here._
<!-- END PLACEHOLDER - ADD NEW CHANGELOG ENTRIES BELOW THIS LINE -->

### What's new

#### Streaming VT500 parser and SGR style model (#1)

{class}`~libvt.parser.Parser` decodes ECMA-48 and VT500 byte streams across
arbitrary chunk boundaries, retaining incomplete UTF-8 sequences and split
escape sequences while clamping oversized parameter lists and string
payloads. {func}`~libvt.parser.parse_sgr` decodes semicolon and ITU T.416
colon subparameters into immutable {class}`~libvt.style.Style`,
{class}`~libvt.style.AnsiColor`, {class}`~libvt.style.IndexedColor`,
{class}`~libvt.style.RgbColor`, and {class}`~libvt.style.UnderlineStyle`
values. See {ref}`architecture` for details.

#### Zero-based screen grid, synchronized frames, and sans-I/O terminal (#1)

{class}`~libvt.terminal.Terminal`, {class}`~libvt.screen.Screen`, and
{class}`~libvt.terminal.Snapshot` expose zero-based `(row, col)` cursor
coordinates and 2D indexing returning lazy {class}`~libvt.screen.Cell`,
{class}`~libvt.screen.RowView`, and {class}`~libvt.screen.RegionView`
views, backed by primary scrollback and alternate-screen switching.
{attr}`~libvt.terminal.Terminal.committed` and
{meth}`~libvt.terminal.Terminal.feed_until` hold mid-frame updates during
DEC mode `?2026` synchronized output, while {class}`~libvt.terminal.Effects`
and {meth}`~libvt.terminal.Terminal.drain_replies` handle `OSC 8`
hyperlinks, `OSC 133` prompt zones, `OSC 7501` program status, `SIXEL` /
Kitty graphics callbacks, and bounded `DA1` / `DA2` / `DSR` / `DECRQM`
replies without performing I/O. See {ref}`sync-and-asyncio` for details.

#### Asyncio stream adapter and pytest assertions (#1)

{class}`~libvt.aio.AsyncTerminalStream` drives a
{class}`~libvt.terminal.Terminal` from `asyncio` streams, coalescing `?2026`
batches up to `sync_timeout` and flushing query replies back to the writer.
{mod}`libvt.pytest_plugin` registers `vt_terminal`, `vt_factory`, and
`vt_parser` fixtures with lazy in-fixture imports, paired with boxed screen
diffs in {func}`~libvt.testing.assert_screen`.
